  "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/3191f16e4c72739688fa4243b44a374a027b307b6e4d419217545e924e1c7a4a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,3-(y-3)^{2}\\le x\\le (y-3)^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{3-(y-3)^{2}}^{(y-3)^{2}+4}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{3-(y-3)^{2}}^{(y-3)^{2}+4}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
